# PLAN-1083 — AV 嵌套模式、守卫与组合（语言共享语料 patterns 面）

The canonical author of the nested-patterns language family. Every case
carries ONE Auto source; the `av` check runs the ordinary AV language
chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`); legacy `VM result` checks keep
their original oracles and owners with the AV-phase `#ignore` marker.

Contract faces (§6 + PATTERN-BIND): the four §6 draft cases verbatim,
nested `is` destructuring with shadowing, guards (evaluated only after
the pattern matched, false falls through to the next arm), or-arms,
wildcards, duplicate/non-exhaustive named rejections and the tuple
across a call boundary.

## Case: nested-result-option
id: "av.parity.1083.nested-result-option"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1083", "patterns"]
links: ["PLAN-1083"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn obtain(ok bool) !?int {
    if ok {
        return Ok(Some(42))
    }
    return Err("bad")
}
fn main() int {
 is obtain(true) {
  Ok(v) -> {
   is v {
    Some(n) -> { return n }
    None -> { return 0 }
   }
  }
  Err(e) -> { return 0 }
 }
}
```

