## Case: nested-is-shadowing
id: "av.parity.1083.nested-is-shadowing"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1083", "patterns"]
links: ["PLAN-1083"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
enum Outer {
    Wrap(int)
}
fn main() int {
    let v = 7
    let o = Outer.Wrap(42)
    is o {
        Outer.Wrap(v) -> {
            return v
        }
    }
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:42
```

### Notes

PATTERN-BIND shadowing: the payload binding `v` shadows the outer `v`
inside the arm scope (returns 42, not 7).

## Case: guard-arm
id: "av.parity.1083.guard-arm"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1083", "patterns"]
links: ["PLAN-1083"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
enum Reg {
    Yes(int)
    No
}
fn main() int {
    let r = Reg.Yes(42)
    is r {
        Reg.Yes(v) if v > 100 -> { return 1 }
        Reg.Yes(v) -> { return v }
        Reg.No -> { return 0 }
    }
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 42

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:42
```

### Notes

PATTERN-BIND guard false continues: the guarded arm shares its disc with
the plain arm; guard false (42 ≤ 100) falls through to the plain Yes arm
(42). A guard after a plain arm stays the frozen duplicate rejection.

## Case: guard-not-evaluated
id: "av.parity.1083.guard-not-evaluated"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1083", "patterns"]
links: ["PLAN-1083"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
enum Reg {
    Yes(int)
    No
}
fn side() bool { print("g")
 return true }
fn main() {
    let r = Reg.No
    is r {
        Reg.Yes(v) if side() -> { print("y") }
        Reg.No -> { print("n") }
    }
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
channel: "unit"

#### stdout

```text
n
```

### Notes

PATTERN-BIND 未选guard不求值: the guard on the UNMATCHED arm never
evaluates (`side()` prints nothing); the No arm runs (`n`).

